From unknown Sun, 23 Sep 2001 11:14:50 -0500
Message-ID: <200109231614.f8NGEi412392@mail.swissonline.ch>
Date: Sun, 23 Sep 2001 11:14:50 -0500
From: Andres Meyer
Subject: pc164 & kernel 2.4.x with sym53c8xx: workaround
In-Reply-To: <200109201213.OAA09851@netcetera.ch>

for a 500Mhz Alpha in a pc164:

aboot.conf:
0:1/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda1 cycle=500000000

This sets the correct clock frequency value (and therefore a working 
udelay(int)). I did not look why it is not set correctly, but without this 
option, bogomips are wrong by a factor of ca. 7 -> all timings are REALLY 
wrong.

Hope it helps,
Andres

PS: this therefore fixes the sym53c8xx no-go and makes it possible to 
actually BOOT ;-)

